From 4c3a2666e64dd093afb7acc3486a2edaf1c26686 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: virtualAxe <virtualaxe@example.invalid>
Date: Mon, 11 May 2026 14:59:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] nerdnos: support virtual low difficulty pools

Why: NerdNos virtual live smoke must interoperate with the same low-difficulty
PublicPool, Bitronics, and Nerdminers pools used by the Bitaxe source. The
upstream NerdNos difficulty path stores the suggested difficulty as an integer
and truncates assigned fractional pool difficulty to zero in the system API.
It also reads suggested difficulty outside the source-native per-pool Stratum
configuration snapshot, so virtual live phases can send a stale integer
suggestion after a fractional difficulty was seeded. Its virtual board
subscribe identity is also rejected by Nerdminer-compatible pools. When
optional extranonce subscribe is disabled, the first submit can also reuse the
optional setup-response ID and be counted as setup instead of an accepted
share.

Virtual-only: the subscribe identity change is limited to the `VIRTUALAXE_GAMMA`
board. Fractional suggested and assigned difficulty preserves existing integer
values and only broadens the Stratum V1/API projection type.

Upstream surface: virtual board identity, Stratum V1 suggested difficulty,
per-pool Stratum config snapshots, assigned pool difficulty projection,
optional setup response ID reservation, and the V1 job validity guard.

Verify: SOURCE=nerdnos make patch-check, SOURCE=nerdnos make verify-submit-replay,
and make verify-release SOURCE=nerdnos.

Removal impact: PublicPool and Bitronics can keep assigning high difficulty
during smoke, Nerdminer-compatible pools reject the subscribe identity, and a
notify without an established extranonce can panic the NerdNos job builder.
Pools that accept the first submitted share can have that response classified
as setup, leaving firmware/API accepted counters unchanged.

